       Option B: Client-Side Generation (Current Implementation)
       - Add JavaScript function to generate sitemap JSON
       - Allow manual export or API endpoint to download
       - Still requires server-side final XML generation
    
    3. PRIORITY GUIDELINES:
       - 1.0 = Homepage (most important)
       - 0.9 = Primary pages (Products, Popular Products)
       - 0.8 = Secondary pages (About, Contact, Events)
       - 0.7 = Individual product/event pages
       - 0.6 = Tertiary pages
       - 0.5 = Low-priority pages
    
    4. CHANGE FREQUENCY GUIDELINES:
       - always = Changes on each request (avoid using)
       - hourly = Changes multiple times per day (cart, listings)
       - daily = Changes daily (product stock, new events)
       - weekly = Changes weekly (new products, events)
       - monthly = Changes infrequently (about us, contact)
       - yearly = Changes rarely (policies, etc.)
       - never = Won't change until date specified
    
    5. PERFORMANCE:
       - Keep main sitemap under 50MB and 50,000 URLs
       - For larger sites, split into multiple sitemaps:
         * sitemap-products.xml (all products)
         * sitemap-events.xml (all events)
         * sitemap-main.xml (core pages)
       - Create sitemap index (sitemap-index.xml) linking to all
    
    6. SUBMISSION:
       - Submit to Google Search Console: https://search.google.com/search-console
       - Submit to Bing Webmaster Tools: https://www.bing.com/webmasters
       - Include sitemap URL in robots.txt (already done)
    
    7. MONITORING:
       - Check Google Search Console for crawl errors
       - Monitor sitemap coverage percentage
       - Track which pages are indexed vs. not indexed
